     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Without addressing how to best do the convoution, I quickly note that &quot;backwards indexing&quot; using a colon (&quot;:&quot;), e.g. indexing a vector as x[10:1], does not work in compiled execution of NIMBLE functions.  My (failing) test case is shown below.</div><div dir=\"ltr\"><br></div><div>Second note, that you *can* do &quot;reverse indexing&quot; of a vector, if the indices themselves are stored in a vector variable.  A (working) example of that is also shown below.</div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br></div><div><font face=\"monospace, monospace\">## FAILING EXAMPLE</font></div><div><div><font face=\"monospace, monospace\">library(nimble)</font></div><div><font face=\"monospace, monospace\"><br></font></div><div><font face=\"monospace, monospace\">Rnf &lt;- nimbleFunction(</font></div><div><font face=\"monospace, monospace\">    run = function(a = double(1)) {</font></div><div><font face=\"monospace, monospace\">        L &lt;- dim(a)[1]</font></div><div><font face=\"monospace, monospace\">        print(&#39;length = &#39;, L)</font></div><div><font face=\"monospace, monospace\">        b &lt;- a[L:1]</font></div><div><font face=\"monospace, monospace\">        print(&#39;reversed vector: &#39;, b)</font></div><div><font face=\"monospace, monospace\">    }</font></div><div><font face=\"monospace, monospace\">)</font></div><div><font face=\"monospace, monospace\"><br></font></div><div><font face=\"monospace, monospace\">Cnf &lt;- compileNimble(Rnf)</font></div><div><font face=\"monospace, monospace\"><br></font></div><div><font face=\"monospace, monospace\">f &lt;- 1:5</font></div><div><font face=\"monospace, monospace\"><br></font></div><div><font face=\"monospace, monospace\">Rnf(f)</font></div><div><font face=\"monospace, monospace\">## length = 5</font></div><div><font face=\"monospace, monospace\">## reversed vector: 5 4 3 2 1</font></div><div><font face=\"monospace, monospace\"><br></font></div><div><font face=\"monospace, monospace\">Cnf(f)</font></div></div><div><div><font face=\"monospace, monospace\">## Process R abort trap: 6 at Fri Aug 31 11:01:27 2018</font></div><div><font face=\"monospace, monospace\">## length = 5</font></div><div><font face=\"monospace, monospace\">## libc++abi.dylib: terminating with uncaught exception of type std::bad_alloc: std::bad_alloc</font></div></div><div><font face=\"monospace, monospace\"><br></font></div><div><font face=\"monospace, monospace\">## WORKING EXAMPLE</font></div><div><font face=\"monospace, monospace\"><div>library(nimble)</div><div><br></div><div>Rnf &lt;- nimbleFunction(</div><div>    run = function(a = double(1)) {</div><div>        L &lt;- dim(a)[1]</div><div>        print(&#39;length = &#39;, L)</div><div>        index &lt;- numeric(L)</div><div>        for(i in 1:L) {</div><div>            index[i] &lt;- L + 1 - i</div><div>        }</div><div>        b &lt;- a[index]</div><div>        print(&#39;reversed vector: &#39;, b)</div><div>    }</div><div>)</div><div><br></div><div>Cnf &lt;- compileNimble(Rnf)</div><div><br></div><div>f &lt;- 1:5</div><div><br></div><div>Rnf(f)</div><div><div>## length = 5</div><div>## reversed vector: 5 4 3 2 1</div></div><div><br></div><div>Cnf(f)</div><div><div>## length = 5</div><div>## reversed vector: 5</div><div>## 4</div><div>## 3</div><div>## 2</div><div>## 1</div><div><br></div></div></font></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div>"
