     "<div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Dear all,<div><br></div><div>I am trying to calculate the sum of two vectors, one of which is reversed. A very direct way works, such as:</div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#008\">for</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">k </span><span style=\"color:#008\">in</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\">K</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  conv</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">k</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  </span><span style=\"color:#008\">for</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">l </span><span style=\"color:#008\">in</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">k</span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    conv</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">k</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">l</span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> conv</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">k</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">l</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> exposure</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">k</span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#000\">l</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]*</span><span style=\"color:#000\">incubationPeriod</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">l</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> <br>  </span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  observed</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">k</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">~</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> dpois</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">conv</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">k</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">k</span><span style=\"color:#660\">])</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span></div></code></div><div><div><br></div><div>However, when I try to vectorize it, the fit gives the wrong result. First way is when I write:</div></div><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#008\">for</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">k </span><span style=\"color:#008\">in</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><font color=\"#006666\"><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span></font><span style=\"color:#660\">:(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">K</span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  </span><span style=\"color:#008\">lambda</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">k</span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> inprod</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">exposure</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">k</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">],</span><span style=\"color:#000\">incubationPeriod</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\">k</span><span style=\"color:#660\">])</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  observed</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">k</span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">~</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> dpois</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#008\">lambda</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">k</span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">])</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span></div></code></div><span style=\"font-family:monospace;background-color:rgb(250,250,250);color:rgb(102,102,0)\"><span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">then the results are not good. </span></span></div><div><span style=\"font-family:monospace;background-color:rgb(250,250,250);color:rgb(102,102,0)\"><span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><br></span></span></div><div><span style=\"font-family:monospace;background-color:rgb(250,250,250);color:rgb(102,102,0)\"><span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">The other way is when I write</span></span></div><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#008\">for</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">k </span><span style=\"color:#008\">in</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">K</span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  </span><span style=\"color:#008\">lambda</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">k</span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><font color=\"#000000\"><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">exposure</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">k</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]%*%</span><span style=\"color:#000\">incubationPeriod</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\">k</span><span style=\"color:#660\">])[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span></font><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><font color=\"#000000\"><span style=\"color:#000\">  observed</span></font><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">k</span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">~</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> dpois</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#008\">lambda</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">k</span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">])</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span></div></code></div><span style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);font-family:monospace;color:rgb(102,102,0)\"><span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">but the kernel dies with the message: </span></span></div><div><span style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">terminate called after throwing an instance of </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;std::bad_alloc&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  what</span><span style=\"color:#660\">():</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  std</span><span style=\"color:#660\">::</span><span style=\"color:#000\">bad_alloc</span></div></code></div><div><br></div></span>My question is whether I am correct in my understanding of the inprod-function and making the reversed vector by &quot;k:1&quot;. And I am also wondering why I have the message from Cpp in the second variant of vectorization.</div><div><br></div><div>Thank you very much for your time in advance.</div><div><br></div><div>ps: I may provide a reproducible example if necessary.</div></div>\r\n\r\n<p></p></blockquote></div>"
