   "date": "2018-09-01T04:08:07Z",
   "subject": "Re: trying to calculate convolution sum in nimble",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Thank you very much! It works as supposed. <div><br></div><div>Finally, I wrote a nimble function for convolution.</div><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><div>nimConvolution = nimbleFunction(</div><div>    run = function(a = double(1), b = double(1)) {</div><div>        L &lt;- dim(a)[1]</div><div>        ans &lt;- inprod(a[L+1-1:L],b)</div><div>        return(ans)</div><div>        returnType(double(0))</div><div>    }</div><div>)</div></div></code></div><div><br></div>However, it worked for that function, but if I would write directly in the code such as:</div><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><div>    for (k in 52:(K-1)) {</div><div>        conv[k+1] &lt;- inprod(exposure[k+1-1:k],incubationPeriod[1:k])</div><div>#         conv[k+1] &lt;- nimConvolution(exposure[1:k],incubationPeriod[1:k]) - top line instead of this line</div><div>        observed[k+1] ~ dpois(conv[k+1])</div><div>    }</div></div></code></div>it would throw me an error:</div><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><pre style=\"box-sizing:border-box;overflow:auto;font-size:14px;padding-top:1px;padding-bottom:1px;line-height:inherit;word-break:break-all;word-wrap:break-word;color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:rgb(255,255,255);border-radius:0px;white-space:pre-wrap;vertical-align:baseline\">Error: Error processing model: something is wrong with the index k_plus_1 - 1:k.</pre></div></code></div></div><div><br><br></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "FmTDcSBzAgAJ",
   "from": "Perry de Valpine",
   "author": "dd632bd3bbcdd7e9",
   "date": "2018-09-05T17:46:47Z",
   "subject": "Re: trying to calculate convolution sum in nimble",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi Andrei,<div><br></div><div>In a nutshell, a decreasing index sequence won&#39;t work in model code.  In this case, it would be desirable for your example to work.  In general, model code needs to be processed more intricately to correctly determine the graph of model relationships, which creates more stringent checking and trapping.   Your workaround with nimConvolution is a good solution.</div><div><br></div><div>A secondary issue is that in model code, the sequence must take the form (start index):(end index).  For example, it can&#39;t take the form &quot;offset + (start index):(end index)&quot;.   We just added a message to that effect to the devel branch yesterday.</div><div><br></div><div>-Perry </div></div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"ltr\">On Fri, Aug 31, 2018 at 9:08 PM Andrei Akhmetzhanov &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">akhmet...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:<br></div></div>"
    ],
